MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 fits my Alexa-enabled TV setup while adding a screen and video calling, giving me a useful new function.",
    "The smart plug feels like a practical extension of my connected home because it would let me control a household device through Alexa."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "More Fire TV sticks repeat something I already have covered with my 4K stick and Fire TV television; neither an HD version nor a themed remote cover gives me a reason to buy again.",
    "Echo Auto and the tablet connect loosely to my electronics purchases, but I have no clear need for in-car Alexa or another way to watch content right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as an ongoing desire for more streaming devices, even though those purchases already meet that need.",
    "My interest in Alexa at home seems to have been extended to Alexa devices in general, although where I would use a device and what it adds matter to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: a useful addition is more appealing than another device that performs the same job without a clear upgrade.",
    "Several voice-control devices appeal to me, but I would choose the Show 8 first because its screen adds a distinct use; liking the others does not mean I need them all."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in connected home devices, but gave too much weight to familiar products and too little to whether they add a useful function."
}
